  "rules": [
    "Dew point above 16°C: run by effort, let pace go. Above 19°C: discard the numbers entirely.",
    "Achilles — two stiff mornings in a row: trim hill sprints and VO2 first, never easy volume.",
    "Every MP session is logged as three numbers: average pace, average HR, and drift between first and second half of the block.",
    "Commute A = 15 km, Commute B = 21 km. Never on Mondays.",
    "Gym A (lower + pull) Monday, Gym B (upper only) Friday PM. Quality and gym legs share days; the day before Sunday stays clean.",
    "When a week goes wrong, cut in this order: Thursday MLR, then Saturday GA, then the quality session. Never cut the Sunday long run. Never make up missed volume the following week.",
    "TSB below -30 means a rest day is the productive call — but it captures cardiovascular load only and overestimates freshness for a musculoskeletal limiter.",
    "Cycling commute does not count toward running volume (~3-4 km running equivalent per leg) but does count toward total fatigue."
  ],
